@meeting train.m7.calder
// Pillar 5, M7 (Day 5, Friday): Calder hands you Torres's old scanner at the board (Torres is off on Fridays) and does
// the first reading. Head writer, seat W. One choice, no wrong answer.
title: Torres's old scanner
from: Chief Ines Calder
gist: Calder gave you Torres's old scanner. It reads a machine's parts, so you can choose which one to fetch.
== lines
calder: Right. Torres is off. He left this for you.   [gesture]
calder > you: His old scanner. There's a note. I didn't read it. I read it.
calder: Hold it to a panel. It reads each part. A bar and a word.
calder: Good, worn, low, failing. One is usually clearly off. That's your part.
calder: Sometimes two read low. Then you use your eyes. The job card, and what you see up close.
calder: Pick wrong and you walk back. That's all. Nobody shouts.
? choice
* How do I tell two low parts apart?   rel:calder+2 flavour:practical
  calder: Look before you scan. A cold door is a seal. A cold oven is an element.   [nod]
* Torres gave me his scanner?   rel:calder+1 flavour:listen
  calder: He did. He'll pretend it was nothing. It wasn't.
* (Turn it over in your hands)
  calder: It's older than you. It still works. Like most of Works.
calder: There's one held for you. I'll read the first. You watch. Then you do one.
